1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,220
Using language

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,280
Reading

3
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:08,020
Chemical or organic farming?

4
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:16,940
Over the past half century, using chemical fertilizers has become very common in farming.

5
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:21,540
Many farmers welcomed them as a great way to stop crop disease

6
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:23,240
and increase production.

7
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:32,460
Recently, however, scientists have been finding that long-term use of these fertilizers can cause damage to the land and,

8
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:35,380
even more dangerous, to people’s health.

9
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:40,560
What are some of the problems caused by chemical fertilizers?

10
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:45,960
First, they damage the land by killing the helpful bacteria

11
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:48,820
and pests as well as the harmful ones.

12
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:54,820
Chemicals also stay in the ground and underground water for a long time.

13
00:00:56,080 --> 00:00:58,240
This affects crops and, therefore,

14
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:04,220
animals and humans, since chemicals get inside the crops and cannot just be washed off.

15
00:01:05,820 --> 00:01:10,640
These chemicals in the food supply build up in people’s bodies over time.

16
00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:15,540
Many of these chemicals can lead to cancer or other illnesses.

17
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:24,980
In addition, fruit, vegetables and other food grown with chemical fertilizers usually grow too fast to be full of much nutrition.

18
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:30,960
They may look beautiful, but inside there is usually more water than vitamins

19
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:31,660
and minerals.

20
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:39,560
With these discoveries, some farmers and many customers are beginning to turn to organic farming.

21
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:44,820
Organic farming is simply farming without using any chemicals.

22
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:49,120
They focus on keeping their soil rich and free of disease.

23
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:54,440
A healthy soil reduces disease and helps crops grow strong

24
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:55,380
and healthy.

25
00:01:56,540 --> 00:01:57,860
Organic farmers, therefore,

26
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:02,000
often prefer using natural waste from animals as fertilizer.

27
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:07,620
They feel that this makes the soil in their fields richer in minerals

28
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:09,180
and so more fertile.

29
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:15,960
This also keeps the air, soil, water and crops free from chemicals.

30
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:22,180
Organic farmers also use many other methods to keep the soil fertile.

31
00:02:23,140 --> 00:02:26,720
They often change the kind of crop in each field every few years,

32
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:32,740
for example, growing corn or wheat and then the next year peas or soybeans.

33
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:39,200
Crops such as peas or soybeans put important minerals back into the soil,

34
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:43,340
making it ready for crops such as wheat or corn that need rich

35
00:02:43,340 --> 00:02:44,860
and fertile soil.

36
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:50,460
Organic farmers also plant crops to use different levels of soil,

37
00:02:50,460 --> 00:02:56,220
for example, planting peanuts that use the ground’s surface followed by vegetables

38
00:02:56,220 --> 00:02:58,200
that put down deep roots.

39
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:06,660
Some organic farmers prefer planting grass between crops to prevent wind or water from carrying away the soil,

40
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:10,420
and then leaving it in the ground to become a natural fertilizer

41
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:12,000
for the next year’s crop.

42
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:17,520
These many different organic farming methods have the same goal:

43
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:22,860
to grow good food and avoid damaging the environment or people’s health.
